  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 106 PM CDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nThe shortwave trough coming out of the southwest U.S will break down \nthe high pressure ridge in east Texas over the weekend..and the \nmulti day heavy rain event will be coming to an end. As this occurs \nwe should see temperatures warm about 10 degrees over the weekend \ninto the upper 80s as we begin to dry out. SPC does have a Day 3 \nMarginal Risk over our eastern areas but this is a low probability \nsituation at this time. Will continue to monitor trends for \nSaturday. In the extended models still showing a trough digging\ninto the southwest US. Differences exist between the ECMWF and \nGFS for next week. The ECMWF wants to pick up the remnants of the \nhurricane and bring the moisture across Texas while the GFS shows \nthe trough missing the hurricane and it slowly wanders in the east\nPacific. In any case cooler temperatures are expected with highs \ndropping back into the 70s to around 80 in the early to middle \nportion of next week. Will continue to monitor trends over the \nnext few days.",
